WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.352 --> 00:00:19.121
The secret garden and bloomed, and every day revealed new miracles.

2
00:00:20.342 --> 00:00:22.083
There were eggs in the robin's nest.

3
00:00:23.244 --> 00:00:25.745
The robin's mate sat upon them until they hatched.

4
00:00:26.986 --> 00:00:30.228
On sunny days the robin watched the children working in the garden.

5
00:00:31.404 --> 00:00:35.105
But on rainy days the robin and his family had the garden to themselves.

6
00:00:38.266 --> 00:00:42.147
One morning when the rain was streaming down, Colin was lying on his sofa.

7
00:00:43.347 --> 00:00:47.408
"Now that I'm a real boy, my arms and legs are so full of magic that I can't

8
00:00:47.448 --> 00:00:48.209
keep them still.

9
00:00:49.389 --> 00:00:51.209
They want to be doing things all the time.

10
00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.450
But it's not safe to get up and walk about.

11
00:00:55.551 --> 00:00:57.291
What do you think would happen if I did that?"

12
00:00:58.852 --> 00:00:59.612
Mary laughed.

13
00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:01.781
"The nurse and Mrs.

14
00:01:01.821 --> 00:01:03.082
Medlock would come running.

15
00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:05.163
They'd send for Dr.

16
00:01:05.223 --> 00:01:06.244
Craven for sure."

17
00:01:06.264 --> 00:01:08.886
"I wish my father would come home.

18
00:01:10.027 --> 00:01:12.909
I don't know how much longer I can go on pretending I'm not well.

19
00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:15.190
I wish it wasn't raining."

20
00:01:16.431 --> 00:01:18.333
It was then that Mary had an idea.

21
00:01:18.353 --> 00:01:21.455
"Do you know how many rooms are in this house?"

22
00:01:23.076 --> 00:01:24.677
Colin guessed about a thousand.

23
00:01:25.838 --> 00:01:28.160
"There are at least a hundred that no one goes into.

24
00:01:29.396 --> 00:01:32.297
I could push you in your wheelchair, and we could visit some of them."

25
00:01:33.457 --> 00:01:34.698
Colin liked that idea.

26
00:01:36.598 --> 00:01:40.139
When they reached the long picture gallery, he sprang from his wheelchair.

27
00:01:40.159 --> 00:01:45.140
"I am going to run from one end of the gallery to the other," he said.

28
00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:48.341
They ran up and down the gallery.

29
00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:52.823
Then they did some strengthening exercises that Dickon had taught them.

30
00:01:54.103 --> 00:01:57.284
After that they wandered through the house opening doors.

31
00:01:59.244 --> 00:02:02.087
They came upon the picture of the girl in the green dress.

32
00:02:02.107 --> 00:02:06.391
"She looks a bit like you, Mary," said Colin.

33
00:02:06.411 --> 00:02:10.435
"Not as you look now, but as you looked when you first came here.

34
00:02:11.536 --> 00:02:13.778
Now you are a great deal fatter and better looking."

35
00:02:13.798 --> 00:02:18.082
"So are you," said Mary, and they both laughed.

36
00:02:21.905 --> 00:02:24.428
Eventually they came back to Colin's room for lunch.

37
00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:31.264
Mary wanted to ask him a question because for several days she'd noticed a change in the room.

38
00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:35.668
The curtain was drawn back to reveal the picture of Colin's mother.

39
00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:41.373
"Two nights ago there was so much moonlight in the room, I woke up," Colin explained.

40
00:02:41.393 --> 00:02:46.857
"A patch of moonlight was shining on the curtain, so I pulled the cord to open it.

41
00:02:47.898 --> 00:02:51.601
My mother was looking right down at me and laughing, as if she were glad to see me

42
00:02:51.661 --> 00:02:52.282
standing there.

43
00:02:53.302 --> 00:02:54.964
I want to see her all the time now.

44
00:02:56.072 --> 00:02:58.473
I think she must have been some sort of magic person."

45
00:02:58.493 --> 00:03:03.096
"Sometimes I think you are her ghost made into a boy."

46
00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:07.058
"If I were her ghost, my father would be fond of me.

47
00:03:08.139 --> 00:03:11.480
Then I could tell him about the magic, and that would make him more cheerful."

48
00:03:12.501 --> 00:03:14.802
"That would be wonderful," said Mary.

49
00:03:16.423 --> 00:03:20.365
The next day the weather cleared, and the children were able to go out into the garden.

50
00:03:21.486 --> 00:03:24.327
Dickon and Mary were busy weeding when Colin called to them.

51
00:03:24.347 --> 00:03:26.508
"Mary! Dickon!

52
00:03:26.989 --> 00:03:27.509
Look at me!"

53
00:03:28.649 --> 00:03:31.131
They stopped working and looked at him, standing there.

54
00:03:31.151 --> 00:03:34.893
"Do you remember that first morning you brought me here?

55
00:03:35.993 --> 00:03:38.675
I was just thinking about that as I was digging with my trowel.

56
00:03:39.836 --> 00:03:43.598
So I had to stand up on my feet once more, to make sure I could really do

57
00:03:43.658 --> 00:03:45.879
it. And it is real!

58
00:03:46.279 --> 00:03:46.779
I'm well!

59
00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:47.900
I'm well!

60
00:03:49.001 --> 00:03:50.982
And I'm going to live forever and ever!"

61
00:03:51.002 --> 00:03:54.924
"Let's sing a song to celebrate," said Mary.

62
00:03:56.684 --> 00:03:58.545
They stood together and sang a hymn.

63
00:03:59.725 --> 00:04:03.466
As the last notes died away, Colin suddenly noticed something.

64
00:04:03.486 --> 00:04:05.346
"Someone's coming!"

65
00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:07.507
He pointed toward the door in the wall.

66
00:04:08.607 --> 00:04:10.948
A woman was entering the secret garden.

67
00:04:12.068 --> 00:04:14.829
Colin had never seen her before, but he wasn't afraid.

68
00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:18.350
Somehow he felt as if he already knew her.

69
00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:21.391
"It's Mother—that's who it is!"

70
00:04:22.551 --> 00:04:25.352
Dickon ran across the grass toward the kind-looking woman.

71
00:04:26.444 --> 00:04:28.665
He brought his mother over to Mary and Colin.

72
00:04:29.645 --> 00:04:32.306
"I told her where the door is because I knew you wanted to meet her."

73
00:04:32.326 --> 00:04:35.188
"Even when I was ill, I wanted to see you."

74
00:04:35.588 --> 00:04:36.668
Colin shook her hand.

75
00:04:38.169 --> 00:04:39.969
"You and Dickon and the secret garden.

76
00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:43.651
I'd never wanted to see anyone or anything before."

77
00:04:43.671 --> 00:04:46.232
"Oh, my dear boy."

78
00:04:46.772 --> 00:04:49.053
Tears filled Susan Sowerby's eyes.

79
00:04:49.073 --> 00:04:52.054
"Are you surprised that I am so well?"

80
00:04:52.554 --> 00:04:53.215
asked Colin.

81
00:04:54.415 --> 00:04:56.096
She put her hand on his shoulder.

82
00:04:57.288 --> 00:05:02.613
"Yes, I am, but you look so much like your mother that it makes my heart jump."

83
00:05:04.074 --> 00:05:05.675
Colin suddenly felt shy.

84
00:05:05.695 --> 00:05:08.818
"Do you think that will make my father like me?"

85
00:05:08.838 --> 00:05:11.220
"Oh, for sure."

86
00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:12.841
She patted his arm.

87
00:05:12.861 --> 00:05:17.245
"Your own dear mother is in this garden, I do believe.

88
00:05:18.406 --> 00:05:19.727
She couldn't keep out of it.

89
00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:25.192
And now your father must come home to see the miracle blooming here."
